So there I was:  playing the best gaem of my short nethack career.
Level 10 Valkyrie, +8 longsword, +5 shield (AC @ -10), coupla
spellbooks of fireball, ring of invisibility, just havin' a heck of a
time.  I had a tinning kit, so I just tinned everything in sight,
because I refuse to run out of food and starve ever again.  I had
about 20 or so tins in my inventory, and, of course, I was "Satiated".
I went to eat a new tin I found, hoping for some spinach.  Now, I know
you can die from overeating, so when it wasn't spinach I decided not
to eat it.  I hit the wrong key and started to eat it.  It asked me:
"Keep eating?  [y/n]"  OK, here's the bug:  I accidently hit space
bar, and it went to the "default setting".  Unfortunately, the
"default" for this situation is keep eating, which killed me.  If you
hit a wrong key and it goes to a default, the default should be
beneficial to the player, not life threatening.  The default should be
stop eating.



